    "created_at": "2026-04-12T07:01:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-12T07:01:25Z",
    "body": "Hi, I’m trying to understand this behavior.\n\nI tested popovers and noticed that when a popover is in the process of hiding, showing another popover at the same time can lead to unclear behavior.\nFrom a user perspective, Option 3 (just letting the new popover show) feels more intuitive, since users expect the latest action to take priority.\nHowever, I’m not sure how this interacts with the existing hide algorithm and whether it could cause inconsistent states.\nWould it make sense to define that showing a new popover cancels or overrides the ongoing hide process of the previous one?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4230958474/reactions",
