    "updated_at": "2026-04-15T23:20:28Z",
    "body": "> Option 1 does have a compat risk. Since it isn't just about `hint`, let's look at it after [#12345](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12345), but I'm happy to spec it up.\n\nI'm really not too concerned about this case. Several (but obviously not all) of these cases already produce a console error in Chromium, and (hopefully) prevent the new popover from showing. Obviously we'll have to roll it out carefully, but I'd prefer a strategy where we get all of these changes nailed down at one time, and ship them as a bundle. That's easier for developers to reason about than a string of changes, any one of which could be breaking. So having said that:\n\n> [@mfreed7](https://github.com/mfreed7) I don't suppose you could add a use-counter to get a feel for how disruptive this would be?\n\nI can do this, but I think I'd prefer to just be the canary here and ship the updated code in Chromium. WDYT? My assumption is that there won't be too many (if any) issues, because all of these (this issue, plus all of #12345) are fairly corner case.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
